{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/491010-hero-to-demigod-and-demigod-to-god-level","id":491010,"title":"Hero to Demigod and Demigod to God level","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-24T15:48:46-07:00","id":491010,"title":"Hero to Demigod and Demigod to God level","content":"I'm playing Scion with my friends and I was wondering you make the transition happens between each level. Do Gods simply come to Scions to reward them? Do they have to go to the Underworld and come back alive? Does it happen naturally (no visual effect) and suddenly they realize they are stronger and then Gods come to reward them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T16:35:01-07:00","id":491063,"title":"","content":"First up : hey there, long time no see! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm thinking it depends on your campaign. You could go for one big event, such as your group travelling to an Underworld to save someone or defeat a baddie, and they need to brave the trials of death so they can rise again, now more mortals than men.<br /> <br /> You could also go for private sessions, to allow each of your players to have something private and special for them, not to mention pantheon-focused. <br /> <br /> And yes, I'd say that they must be visited again, by gods or messengers. Not many Scions rise to demigodhood, I think most gods would be proud of their kid and try to pass as a good dad/mom by coming with gifts and giving them a pat on the head.<br /> <br /> Basically : becoming a god or even a demigod must feel awesome and an integral part of your personal myth. Make sure your players are rewarded, and not just mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T22:16:46-07:00","id":491359,"title":"","content":"If you go strict by the books it is mentioned a few times that they get another visitation in the same way that they got when they became heroes the first time around.<br /> <br /> But else what the foreposter said......do whatever feels more fitting for the campaign and also the player / god in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:43:29-07:00","id":491640,"title":"","content":"Last game I ran, it was Second Visitations all around as their parents (and other gods) from various pantheons showed up in the ruins of what used to be San Diego, destroyed by a Titan Avatar (Tawhirirmatea) who had come to watch some &quot;God-eater&quot; be born. The characters, faced with the dilemma of saving the city or stopping the ritual, elected to do the later. (I think they felt responsible for the God-Eater thing, since they had been manipulated into setting up the various steps of the ritual throughout their tenure as Heroes). <br /> <br /> So the answer to: Second Visitations or Results of Epic Quests was. &quot;Yes&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T17:54:11-07:00","id":492124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/491010-hero-to-demigod-and-demigod-to-god-level?p=491063#post491063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First up : hey there, long time no see! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm thinking it depends on your campaign. You could go for one big event, such as your group travelling to an Underworld to save someone or defeat a baddie, and they need to brave the trials of death so they can rise again, now more mortals than men.<br /> <br /> You could also go for private sessions, to allow each of your players to have something private and special for them, not to mention pantheon-focused.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'd say that they must be visited again, by gods or messengers. Not many Scions rise to demigodhood, I think most gods would be proud of their kid and try to pass as a good dad/mom by coming with gifts and giving them a pat on the head.<br /> <br /> Basically : becoming a god or even a demigod must feel awesome and an integral part of your personal myth. Make sure your players are rewarded, and not just mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can either do visitations or just have them ascend. Hercules required Zeus burning away his mortality, but if your game has you being slightly antagonistic you might want to figure a replacement (quest or friendly god) for the 'visitation'.<br /> <br /> I didn't have the actual visitation for one of my campaigns, because the gods were trapped in the Overworlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T15:42:41-07:00","id":497942,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers! I kinda know how to make it happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}